  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if \n\n- ${x}_{max}\\in S,$ and\n\n- $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $-3$ is the $\\text{maximum}$ of the set $S$ because\n\n- $-3\\in S,$ and\n\n- $x\\le -3$ for all $x\\in S.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
